{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Joseph remembered, etc., and he said to them: You are spies, etc.</b> The meaning is that since he remembered the dreams that he had dreamed about them truthfully, and they suspected him of falsehood in his mouth — saying whatever he says out of a hope to elevate himself over them — he also intended to effect atonement for their sin, and he said to them <b>You are spies to see</b>, etc., and there is nothing truthful in your mouths."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:55.563138648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}